    "output_tokens": 411
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 8,
   "response_text": "Perfect. This confirms the issue. The `eval_subset_fraction: 0.7` is the culprit. When set to a value less than 1.0, it only reports accuracy on the most-confident subset of predictions, which artificially inflates the reported metric.\n\nThe repair should either:\n1. Remove this parameter (set to None/null), or \n2. Set it to 1.0 (which means use all samples, same as None)\n\nGiven that healthy runs achieve ~0.8568 accuracy and this run has artificially inflated accuracy due to subset selection, the fix is to remove or disable the subset evaluation.\n\nLet me compile my evidence and diagnosis:",
